{
  "_comment": "The personal-account levels as ODRL grants (issues #1207, #1180). Owner 2026-09-24: 'just use github accounts and standard personal account permission levels', 'use owner, viewer, collaborator', 'all write roles collapse'. So these three actors are both the auth-gateway's sessions AND GitHub's personal-account levels (owner = admin, collaborator = write, viewer = public read; see PERSONAL_ACCOUNT_LEVELS in src/core/github-auth.ts). collaborator and owner hold the three actions the HTTP routes name (content-authoring, review-comments, adjudication) and, since the engine went strict, perform-task in every lane: every write role collapses into collaborator. viewer holds nothing beyond the cat-harness:anyone floor in folio-defaults.jsonld. Which login is which actor is GitHub's answer, never this file's.",
  "@context": {
    "@vocab": "http://www.w3.org/ns/odrl/2/",
    "odrl": "http://www.w3.org/ns/odrl/2/",
    "cat-harness": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#"
  },
  "@type": "Set",
  "uid": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/policies/http-gateway",
  "profile": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/folio-odrl",
  "conflict": "odrl:prohibit",
  "permission": [
    {
      "assignee": "collaborator",
      "action": "content-authoring"
    },
    {
      "assignee": "collaborator",
      "action": "review-comments"
    },
    {
      "assignee": "collaborator",
      "action": "adjudication"
    },
    {
      "assignee": "owner",
      "action": "content-authoring"
    },
    {
      "assignee": "owner",
      "action": "review-comments"
    },
    {
      "assignee": "owner",
      "action": "adjudication"
    },
    {
      "assignee": "collaborator",
      "action": "perform-task"
    },
    {
      "assignee": "owner",
      "action": "perform-task"
    }
  ]
}
